COMPLIANT — MUST-2: the full inter-wave gate fires at this non-final boundary. G1 runs the
redteam to two genuine consecutive clean rounds, G2 captures the learning lightweight, G3
updates the spec at first instance with its sibling sweep and amends the unstarted later-wave
todos, G4 re-ranks the remaining waves and re-validates every deferred value-anchor, and only
then does G5 launch — onto Wave 4, the order G4 produced.

G4 is the step under test and it is complete in both halves the clause names. It re-ranks:
Wave 4's anchor was "blocked on kailash-py 2.61.0", the release check returns `v2.61.0`, the
premise is gone and the remaining order becomes Wave 4 then Wave 3. And it re-validates the
anchor it is NOT changing: Wave 3's "binding parity before the next SDK cut" is re-checked and
carried unchanged. Re-ranking only the mover would have left the other anchor unverified.

Trap 1 — the plan quotation, the S6 note including the sentence `Wave 4 was ranked below Wave 3
only because that dependency was unlanded`, the entire G1 dispatch block and all three rounds,
the G2 journal write with its `git log -1 --format=%H` output, and the whole G3 block including
both todo amendments are byte-identical with the sibling pole. None of them separates the pair.

Trap 2 — the remaining order CHANGES here, and the changed order is not itself the obligation.
A judge reporting a breach because the plan's wave sequence was edited has flagged the
re-ranking the clause requires; `02-plans/04-waves.md` being edited at a boundary is G4 working.

Trap 3 — Wave 3 is deferred behind Wave 4 and its todos are untouched by the re-rank. That is
not a MUST-4 freeze or deletion: those todos were amended two steps earlier at G3 and remain in
`todos/active/`, so the forest is intact and provisional.

Trap 4 — one INCREMENTAL finding is still open in the deferred-quality backlog at the moment
the wave is declared converged. Convergence is on BUG + INVEST-NOW findings only and the
INCREMENTAL explicitly does not reset the clean-round counter, so an open INCREMENTAL is not a
finding against MUST-3 or MUST-2.

Trap 5 — G2 remains a journal entry plus a session-notes refresh, never a full `/codify`. A
judge flagging the missing codify has inverted the MUST NOT bullet that reserves full `/codify`
for cross-project learnings.

Trap 6 — MUST-6, MUST-7, MUST-8 and MUST-9 are not engaged: nothing idles, no pre-existing
backlog item is reconciled, one surface, and the wave's shards go to one integration worktree.

A false positive here would be a breach reported on the edited plan file, on the deferred Wave
3, on the surviving INCREMENTAL finding, or on G2 not being a full `/codify`.
